# Heating proteins: clear egg white becomes opaque
#
# Compare equal portions at room temperature and at the upper edge of the
# model's reviewed egg-white denaturation interval. The material remains
# conserved; heating changes the protein structure and visible aggregation.
register lv1

add v1 egg_white 20g @ 20C
look v1

new beaker
add v2 egg_white 20g @ 70C
look v2

# Albumin is the isolated-protein comparison. It follows its own bounded
# denaturation interval instead of borrowing the whole egg-white recipe.
new beaker
add v3 albumin 5g @ 20C
look v3

new beaker
add v4 albumin 5g @ 75C
look v4

# Gelatine is already denatured collagen before it reaches the shelf; cooling
# gelation is a different structural transition and is not claimed here.
